{
 "about": "NAMES ONLY, for core/banter_memory.py: the personal weapons, armor sets, commodities, ship components, item makers, vehicles and plushies the game has, so that a sentence naming one is read as game talk and not as 'a name from outside the game'. No prices, no stats, no ids. A name here is evidence that a sentence is about the game; it never gets a sentence past the veto.",
 "source": "SC Toolbox Market_Finder UEX cache (skills/Market_Finder/.uex_cache.json, lists 'items' and 'vehicles'; data from the uexcorp.space API), cache written 2026-10-04",
 "copied": "2026-10-05",
 "method": "Copied by a hand-run script, not imported across tools (the cache is a local file that git ignores, so it is not on every machine). Personal weapons (section 'Personal Weapons'), armor (sections 'Armor' and 'Undersuits'), components (the categories named below) and plushies (section 'Miscellaneous', names holding 'Plushie'): the FIRST WORD of the item name, so Zenith \"Thunderstrike\" Laser Sniper Rifle gives Zenith and Geist Backpack Forest gives Geist. Commodities: the whole name without '(Ore)' or '(Raw)'. Makers: company_name of those rows. Vehicles: every vehicle name. Clothing, liveries, food, drink, decorations and attachments were left out: their names are mostly ordinary words and colours. banter_memory.py drops ordinary words, first names and anything the veto knows when it reads this.",
 "credit": "Item and vehicle names: UEX (uexcorp.space). Star Citizen content (c) Cloud Imperium Games; not affiliated.",
